# CANONICAL DEPLOYED REFS -- the single source of truth for "what is on chain".
#
# Consumed by BOTH:
#   .github/workflows/ci.yml   (sibling checkout pins)
#   scripts/parity-check.sh    (cross-program constant comparison)
#
# It exists because the two used to disagree and nothing noticed: CI pinned the nft
# sibling at f18da24 while cf56ba5 was what devnet actually ran, so the five-program
# crosscut suite tested a build that is not deployed and the on-chain regression was
# structurally invisible. A pin that lives in exactly one place cannot drift from itself.
#
# Values are quoted from ~/percolator-ops/ledger/deployments.md (devnet, P5 2026-08-27):
#
#   | wrapper     | percolator-prog    | DhSkE7u... | 15eb8b0c |   (2026-08-31, #441)
#   | vault/stake | percolator-stake   | GCHhcgw... | d0c6ecb  |   (2026-08-31, #441)
#   | nft         | percolator-nft     | CNGBPZR... | cf56ba5  |
#   | matcher     | percolator-matcher | 4seJWjv... | d4d4f1c  |   (repo dir: percolator-match)
#
# Refs MUST be full 40-character SHAs: actions/checkout resolves `ref` with
# `git fetch origin <ref>`, and an abbreviated SHA is not a valid fetch refspec. Every
# CI run between the pins being added and 2026-08-24 died on exactly that.

# --- deployed, i.e. the bytes running on devnet right now -------------------------------
WRAPPER_DEPLOYED=15eb8b0c599e35a1c224bfa74f92b810c78fefb7
STAKE_DEPLOYED=d0c6ecb0e063ddd024ae33afce5a43a16242aeda
NFT_DEPLOYED=215842ecf8f4683de8e0915010d1f74f1060ead3
MATCHER_DEPLOYED=d4d4f1c40efb37cbcf44e42b99a46d49c32c4dca

# --- CI SIBLINGS: what the wrapper SHIPS AGAINST. *NOT* what is on chain. ----------------
#
# Read this block as the opposite of the one above. Everything named *_DEPLOYED is a
# statement about the chain and must never be moved to make a job green. Everything named
# *_CI_SIBLING is a statement about THIS TREE: the sibling commit this wrapper source is
# written to compile and pass against. They are equal in the steady state and differ only
# across a flag day, i.e. between "merged" and "deployed".
#
# ENGINE_CI_SIBLING -- the engine ci.yml's `test` job checks out for the `path = "../percolator"`
# dependency. There was no engine pin at all until 2026-09-15: ci.yml checked the engine out
# at whatever dcccrypto/percolator main happened to be. On 2026-09-09 engine main took
# bf2fda46 (upstream 92ed4a1a, "layout 18"), which added PortfolioLegV16::kf_epoch_snap, and
# every prog PR from then on failed `build + test` with `error[E0063]: missing field
# kf_epoch_snap` in tests/v16_wrapper.rs -- a file none of those PRs touched. The last green
# `build + test` on this repo is 2026-09-05. A cross-repo dependency that is not pinned does
# not test "what we ship"; it makes every PR's verdict a function of another repo's merge
# queue that hour.
#
#   a90fb27f = dcccrypto/percolator main, 2026-09-15. Layout 18, and the release-gate fixes
#   on top of candidate 2c38570a: F-04 9de7eb9d, F-03 9d3ceec5/b7e76dcb,
#   F-02 b0e110cd/ad463472/22440ebb, I2+K a90fb27f.
#
# WHAT IS ON CHAIN IS A DIFFERENT COMMIT. ~/percolator-ops/ledger/deployments.md records the
# live wrapper as built against engine `9483ee90` (layout 17). That commit is deliberately NOT
# added here as an ENGINE_DEPLOYED pin: this tree cannot be built against it at all (the
# layout-18 fields do not exist there), so a pin nothing can consume would be decoration, and
# the ledger is the authority on the chain. Moving ENGINE_CI_SIBLING is a deliberate reviewable
# commit that re-runs the suite against the new engine -- an engine bump showing up as a diff
# instead of as a mystery red job on someone else's PR.
#
# Upstream aeyakovenko/percolator-prog pins the same thing in-tree instead: it consumes the
# engine as `percolator = { git = "...", rev = "394fd0bf2cb7d73df425eb3754dc3be1a0c44336" }`
# in Cargo.toml (both the main and the `cfg(not(target_os = "solana"))` dependency), and has
# no CI at all. Our fork uses `path = "../percolator"` so the two repos can be edited in
# lockstep, which is what moves that pin into this file.
#
#   c141d47f = dcccrypto/percolator main, 2026-09-16 (batch/wrapper-v19). Descends from
#   a90fb27f with the fixes the release gate needed at the time this batch was assembled:
#   dc01e542 Q+Q2 (lapsed-backing expiry), 72289b24 test hygiene (H-1/AS-03/AS-05/H-2/H-3/
#   AS-04), 3c71bdc3 F-02 (kernel_settle_close_ledger_principal Kani harnesses),
#   ec4fe432 F-04-L (dead-leg forfeit gate widened to the DrainOnly wind-down arm),
#   d61912bb C-S-04 (impaired counterparty lien no longer supports the certificate,
#   converges with upstream faa3bcf9), c141d47f KANI-NSLC (kernel_normalize_social_loss_carry
#   harness). Bumped for batch/wrapper-v19 (WRAPPER-BATCH, 2026-09-16) so the batch's `test`
#   job measures against the engine that actually carries these fixes instead of the stale
#   a90fb27f pin.
ENGINE_CI_SIBLING=c141d47fad9b745e9f855649b1999aecce07bd86
#
# NFT_CI_SIBLING -- the nft ci.yml's `test` job mounts as a sibling .so. Equal to NFT_DEPLOYED
# in the steady state; it is 74293a2e (nft main after #196) only for the length of the
# layout-18 flag day. Under the layout-18 engine the wrapper's portfolio account is 9,539 B,
# and the deployed nft 215842e vendors a 9,227-B mirror whose `decode_portfolio` length gate
# rejects the account before VERSION is read, so that pair cannot pass anything -- measured:
# 5 v16_nft_e2e + 2 v16_five_program_crosscut failures with 215842e, 0 with 74293a2e.
# Bumping NFT_DEPLOYED instead was measured to turn the `parity` job red on
# `DEPLOYED nft.header_version` (deployed wrapper 15eb8b0c stamps VERSION 17, nft 74293a2e
# wants 18) and would be a false statement about the chain besides: 74293a2e is merged, not
# deployed. DELETE this line and revert ci.yml's nft ref to NFT_DEPLOYED the moment the nft
# and the wrapper deploy together and NFT_DEPLOYED moves to that commit.
NFT_CI_SIBLING=74293a2e26e6e61eeb7b2ddc6b55f70d9de7c9db

# --- the nft build that is CORRECT but NOT deployed -------------------------------------
# f18da24 is the tip of percolator-nft `feat/accept-wrapper-version-17`, preserved on the
# remote as branch `deployed/nft-f18da24`. It was the PREVIOUSLY deployed nft; it carries
# ce6b051 ("accept wrapper VERSION 17") and 58911ab ("point wrapper allowlist at the fresh
# devnet wrapper ID"), neither of which was ever merged to nft main. The P5 deploy shipped
# nft main (cf56ba5) over it and REVERTED both fixes on chain.
#
# CI runs the suite against BOTH pins -- see the `nft_pin` matrix in ci.yml.
# CONVERGED 2026-08-29. NFT_FIX was the unmerged branch carrying the two fixes; they are now
# merged to nft main AND deployed, so NFT_DEPLOYED already contains them and this axis no
# longer distinguishes anything. Kept only as the historical record of what was missing.
NFT_FIX_HISTORICAL=f18da240677c390adb74285d03b2bbdc9e1dfef1

# --- program ids ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The wrapper's `declare_id!` is the placeholder `Perco1ator111...`; the real id comes from
# the deploy keypair, so it cannot be read out of the source and has to be pinned here.
WRAPPER_PROGRAM_ID_DEVNET=DhSkE7uTb8HBUYYWF1xkxMYBGtLYJEoDq1tfBD7SnHcj
WRAPPER_PROGRAM_ID_MAINNET=ESa89R5Es3rJ5mnwGybVRG1GrNt9etP11Z5V2QWD4edv

# --- 2026-08-31: the #441 coordinated bump -----------------------------------------------
# WRAPPER_DEPLOYED and STAKE_DEPLOYED moved TOGETHER, and they must always move together.
# The wrapper pins StakePool v4/408 exclusively; stake d0c6ecb emits it. Advancing one pin
# without the other makes CI build a wrapper that rejects every pool its own sibling stake
# creates (Custom(9) at tag 87), or a stake whose pools the wrapper refuses on length.
#
# percolator-gate test/20 cross-checks these values against
# ~/percolator-ops/ledger/deployments.md on every run. It is what caught this file still
# pinning 474079f after the deploy — exactly the drift the header above says cannot happen
# when a pin lives in one place. It can: one place still has to be UPDATED.
